  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Cooptado’s victory in the 2015 Singapore Gold Cup was an international success for Valentin Bukhtoyarov’s racing interests. The Russian businessman owned the Argentine-bred horse with Evgeny Kappushev through Red Stable. Trained by Patrick Shaw, Cooptado had already competed in Argentina and Dubai before winning at Kranji.\n\nBukhtoyarov’s involvement extended beyond buying horses to breeding them. Royal Word was bred for him at France’s Haras du Quesnay, while he kept Arabian broodmares at Haras du Berlais for horses racing principally in Russia. His runners competed across Europe and the United States. Major meetings also provided an occasion to share his enthusiasm with friends; in Russia, he sponsored an entire racing programme.",
    "html": "<p>Cooptado’s victory in the 2015 Singapore Gold Cup was an international success for Valentin Bukhtoyarov’s racing interests. The Russian businessman owned the Argentine-bred horse with Evgeny Kappushev through Red Stable. Trained by Patrick Shaw, Cooptado had already competed in Argentina and Dubai before winning at Kranji.</p>\r\n<p>Bukhtoyarov’s involvement extended beyond buying horses to breeding them. Royal Word was bred for him at France’s Haras du Quesnay, while he kept Arabian broodmares at Haras du Berlais for horses racing principally in Russia. His runners competed across Europe and the United States. Major meetings also provided an occasion to share his enthusiasm with friends; in Russia, he sponsored an entire racing programme.</p>\r\n",
